{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Lift up the head.</b> That which He commanded to count them now — our Rabbis of blessed memory compared it to a parable of a shepherd into whose flock wolves entered and killed some of them, and he counts them to know how many remain. And furthermore, at first they were counted when they came out of Egypt; now that the time of his death has arrived and he must return his sheep to their Owner, he returns them by count." "<b>To their fathers' houses.</b> He traces their lineage after the tribe of the father and not after the tribe of the mother."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:10.465436386Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}